      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\frac{2}{5}m+8-\\frac{6}{5}m-3=$",
      "worked_solution": "We collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}m+8-\\frac{6}{5}m-3 & = \\\\ (\\frac{2}{5}m-\\frac{6}{5}m)+(8-3) & = \\\\ (\\frac{2-6}{5})m+5 & = \\\\ -\\frac{4}{5}m+5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
